{"segs": ["PA_ja_26:0.2", "PA_ja_26:0.3"], "en": "The First Book, The Section on Antelopes (Kuruṅgavagga)", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_26:0.4"], "en": "6. The Mahilāmukha Jātaka:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_26:1.1", "PA_ja_26:1.2"], "en": "“Having listened to the words of the old thieves, Mahilāmukha followed along, striking them.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_26:1.3"], "en": "\"For by attending to the words of those who are well-restrained,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_26:1.4"], "en": "the noblest of elephants stands firm in all virtues.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_26:2.1"], "en": "Thus ends the sixth Jātaka, the Mahilāmukha-jātaka.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"}
